The MIT License in LICENSE covers the work authored in this repository:

    minichess_agent.py    the agent
    baseline_agent.py     the earlier version of the agent, kept as a baseline
    tournament_match.py   the match runner and score card for the tournament rules
    tests/                the test suite
    tools/render_demo.py  the screenshot generator
    README.md             the write-up
    ENGINEERING.md        the long-form write-up

It does not cover the game engine, match runner and sample opponents, which are
third party and keep whatever terms they were released under:

    board.py
    config.py
    game_runner.py
    docs/GameEngine.md
    p22cs201.py
    p25cs0004.py

Those files originate from
github.com/Divyaanshmertia/AI-Assignment-Spartans-Chess-Tournament-2.0
and are included essentially unmodified so the agent can actually be run. The
only change is to game_runner.py, whose imports and default matchup were
repointed at the agents in this repository. Its scoring is untouched, and
differs from the tournament rules that tournament_match.py implements; README.md
sets out both.
